  "details": "**Title:** \"Website Does Not Reflect 'Appear as User' Visual Rank Setting\"\n\n**Description:**  \n\nThe \"Appear as User\" setting, which is available in the VRChat application, does not reflect correctly on the VRChat website. This setting allows users with ranks from \"Known User\" and above to toggle their displayed rank to appear as a \"User\" for personal or privacy reasons. While this change is applied correctly in-game, the website continues to display the actual rank of the user (e.g., Known User, Trusted User), even after logging in.\n\n**Steps to Reproduce:**  \n\n1. Log in to the VRChat application.  \n\n2. Enable the \"Appear as User\" option by clicking your trust rank below your status.  \n\n3. Log in to the VRChat website and navigate to your profile page.  \n\n4. Observe that the rank displayed on the website does not update to \"User.\"  \n\n**Expected Behavior:**  \n\nWhen the \"Appear as User\" setting is enabled in the VRChat application, the website should display the user's rank as \"User\" to match the in-game setting.\n\n**Actual Behavior:**  \n\nThe website continues to display the user's true rank (e.g., Known User, Trusted User) rather than reflecting the \"Appear as User\" setting applied in-game.\n\n**Additional Details:**  \n\n- The issue is specific to the website and does not impact the functionality of the setting within the application.  \n\n- This inconsistency may lead to confusion for users who expect their website profile to align with their in-game settings.",
